{#
    One article, with its sidebar of related posts and its comment thread.

    A SHELL, like the index. <custom-falak-blog-article> reads
    GET /api/storefront/blogs/{slug} for the article — that endpoint is also
    what bumps view_count — and GET /api/storefront/blogs for the sidebar.
    The thread under the article is <custom-falak-blog-comments>, which the
    article element renders itself.

    | slug | string | the route parameter, handed down so the element does not |
    |      |        | have to re-parse the URL                                 |

    The <title>, description, canonical and Article JSON-LD come from the
    server (StorefrontController::blogShow reads the SEO columns), so nothing
    here prints them.
#}
{% extends "layouts.master" %}

{% block content %}
    <div class="container blog-post">
        <custom-falak-blog-article slug="{{ slug }}"></custom-falak-blog-article>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
